# Drafted by Gemini (R16 queue), edited.

~ morgan_start
morgan [weary]: My kettles only hold so much bitter-root, and three folk wait on the cobbles outside. Could you look them over and tell me who needs the draught first?
Narrator: Steam curls from a cracked earthen pot, thick with the sharpness of boiled yarrow and vinegar.
* We will see to it. -> accept
* Not now. -> END

~ accept
morgan [smile]: Bless your boots. Take a slow look before you choose, if you would.
set queue_asked
quest quarantine_queue asked
-> END

~ haldor
haldor_vane [weary]: Good evening to you, strangers. Do not mind my shivering, I have stood in worse damp than this, and I will wait my proper turn without a fuss.
Narrator: The old cooper grips his ash stave with both hands to stop their trembling, though his knuckles knock against the wood.
* [Medicine DC 12] Look at his symptoms -> haldor_med | haldor_nomed
* Take our leave -> haldor_end

~ haldor_med
Narrator: His skin burns like a kiln brick through his wool coat, and beneath his left ribs a swollen knot shifts with a slow, squirming pulse.
set queue_medic_read
-> haldor_end

~ haldor_nomed
Narrator: He is an old man sweating through a heavy fever, though you cannot tell how deep the rot goes.
-> haldor_end

~ haldor_end
set haldor_talked
if flag.haldor_talked and flag.ottilie_talked and flag.pim_talked
set queue_talked
endif
-> END

~ ottilie
ottilie_reed [angry]: You there, tell the apothecary I am next in through that door! Somebody has to shout on this step, or a mother and her babe will freeze in the fog!
Narrator: She bounces a swaddled infant on one hip, her voice hoarse and raw against the damp night.
* [Medicine DC 12] Look at the baby and her bites -> ottilie_med | ottilie_nomed
* Take our leave -> ottilie_end

~ ottilie_med
Narrator: Two mauve welts fester along her forearm, hot and ugly, but her breathing is steady and the sleeping babe's skin is wholly unmarked.
-> ottilie_end

~ ottilie_nomed
Narrator: She is a loud, tired young woman with dark rings under her eyes and a fretful bundle in her arms.
-> ottilie_end

~ ottilie_end
set ottilie_talked
if flag.haldor_talked and flag.ottilie_talked and flag.pim_talked
set queue_talked
endif
-> END

~ pim
pim_fenwick [smile]: Ah, splendid, the stewards have arrived. I am Pim Fenwick, Mayor Somerton's own cousin on the mother's side, so you may show me straight to the front.
Narrator: He adjusts an immaculate silk cravat with two gloved fingers, smelling strongly of lavender water.
* Ask why he thinks so -> pim_why
* [Medicine DC 12] Look at his symptoms -> pim_med | pim_nomed
* Take our leave -> pim_end

~ pim_why
pim_fenwick [sly]: Why, for the sake of civic order, my dear friend. If the cousin of the gavel falls to the sniffles, who will witness the parish ledgers?
-> pim

~ pim_med
Narrator: Aside from a tiny red spot on his wrist and a theatrical sniffle, he is in rude health and has clearly dressed for the occasion.
-> pim_end

~ pim_nomed
Narrator: He looks well-dressed and slightly flushed from the night air, nothing more you can say.
-> pim_end

~ pim_end
set pim_talked
if flag.haldor_talked and flag.ottilie_talked and flag.pim_talked
set queue_talked
endif
-> END

~ morgan_order
morgan [neutral]: The draught is strained and cooling in the cup. How shall I call them in from the step?
-> order_menu

~ order_menu
* Ask Morgan for the list -> list
* Haldor, then Ottilie, then Pim -> fair
* Ottilie first, she is loudest -> loud
* Pim first, the mayor's cousin -> rank
* [ends:quarantine_queue] Let them sort it out themselves -> walk_away

~ list
morgan [weary]: If my own eyes serve, old Haldor is burning through his wick, Ottilie has the spots on her arm, and Master Pim mostly has a fright. Haldor, then Ottilie, then Pim.
-> order_menu

~ fair
morgan [smile]: That sits right with me. Come in out of the cold, Master Vane, and lean on my shoulder.
Narrator: Old Haldor drinks the steaming cup first, and before the hour is out his ragged breathing settles into a deep, quiet sleep.
set queue_outcome = "fair"
set queue_done
quest quarantine_queue done
gold +30
-> END

~ loud
morgan [sad]: If that is the peace we must keep, then send her in. I only hope the old cooper's heart holds while the second kettle boils.
Narrator: Ottilie sweeps inside first, while out in the fog Haldor leans harder on his stave, his fever climbing in silence.
set queue_outcome = "loud"
set queue_haldor_worse
set queue_done
quest quarantine_queue done
-> END

~ rank
morgan [weary]: Custom is custom in Wickermoor, I suppose. Send Master Fenwick to the chair, and tell the others to wrap their cloaks tight.
Narrator: Pim strolls inside to warm his boots and Mayor Somerton will hear of your courtesy, though on the cobbles old Haldor's fever climbs without a word of complaint.
set queue_outcome = "rank"
set queue_haldor_worse
standing old_ways +1
set queue_done
quest quarantine_queue done
-> END

~ walk_away
morgan [sad]: Ah. I do not have the voice for shouting over them, truth be told.
Narrator: Morgan lets out a small sigh as the step outside breaks into bitter shouting, and by the next dawn black mourning ribbons hang from a door in the Round.
set queue_outcome = "lost"
set queue_lost
set queue_done
quest quarantine_queue lost
-> END
